// sc4sap:graph — one call for the stocker flow's Step G: graph.json (+ usage) for one package.
//
//   node build-package-graph.mjs --dir <inventory dir> --src <MCP output src dir> [--system S] [--sap-version ECC|S4]
//
// <inventory dir> holds walk.json (required) and, when collected, tcodes.json (GetTransaction result),
// ddic.json ({ fields: DD03L rows, dtels: DD04L rows }) or ddic-facts.md (Step G3 checker FACT lines),
// and usage.json ({ tcodes, jobs }).
// <MCP output src dir> is where GetProgFullCode output:"file" saved the sources (<name>.prog/, <name>.fugr/).
// Only folders of PROG / FUGR members are read — other programs in the shared output dir are ignored.
// Writes graph.json, and usage-result.json + usage.md when usage.json exists. Prints a JSON summary.

import { existsSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join, resolve } from 'node:path';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
import { parseDdicFacts } from './ddic-edges.mjs';
import { discoverUnits, extractGraph } from './extract-edges.mjs';
import { loadGraph, toMarkdown, usage } from './graph-query.mjs';

const readJson = (p) => (existsSync(p) ? JSON.parse(readFileSync(p, 'utf8')) : null);

// sc4sap:graph — repository facts that source parsing cannot see, turned into edges.
//
//   TCodes  (TSTC / TSTCP via GetTransaction) → TRAN launches PROG, or the SM30 view / t-code
//           a parameter transaction opens
//   DDIC    (DD03L / DD04L rows via GetSqlQuery) → TABL/STRU/VIEW types DTEL (field typing),
//           TABL/STRU types STRU (.INCLUDE / .APPEND), DTEL types DOMA
//
// Only customer objects (Z*, Y*, /namespace/) and listed members become DDIC targets: a
// standard data element on a Z table adds nothing to "which CBO objects are used".
//
// Shapes accepted:
//   tcodes: [{ tcode, program }] · { TCODE: PROGRAM } · GetTransaction result
#!/usr/bin/env node
// sc4sap:graph — TCode / job usage measured on ANOTHER system (QA, PRD), submitted by the user as a file.
//
// The live tools (GetTcodeUsage / GetJobUsage) only see the connected system. On a DEV profile that is
// developer testing, not business use. This script takes whatever the user exported or pasted
// (ST03N transaction profile → spreadsheet / local file, SM37 list, or one name per line), keeps the
// names that are members of the package, and writes the `tcodes` (or `jobs`) side of usage.json.
//
//   node import-usage.mjs --dir <inventory dir> --file <export> --system <SID> [--months 12] [--kind tcodes|jobs]
//
// Formats: .xlsx (cell text), any text (.txt / .csv / .tsv / unconverted list). Names are matched
// case-insensitively against walk.json → objects[] (TRAN for tcodes, PROG for jobs); everything else
diff --git a/skills/sap-option/SKILL.md b/skills/sap-option/SKILL.md
index 852aad7..4163099 100644
--- a/skills/sap-option/SKILL.md
+++ b/skills/sap-option/SKILL.md
@@ -83,6 +83,9 @@ RFC backend (optional — selects transport for Screen / GUI Status / Text Eleme

 Per-backend env blocks (Native / Gateway / OData credentials and knobs) live in [`rfc-managed-keys.md`](rfc-managed-keys.md). Read that file when the user asks to change the RFC backend or edit any `SAP_RFC_*` field.

+Usage statistics source (optional, ECC — read by the CBO graph step and `GetTcodeUsage`):
+- `SAP_USAGE_RFCDEST` — SM59 destination on THIS system pointing to the QA / PRD system whose ST03N usage counts (a DEV profile only sees developer tests). Site-specific — no default; validate by one `GetTcodeUsage` call with `destination` (success shows the remote SID). Empty / unset → the connected system.
+
 XSUAA (only when `SAP_AUTH_TYPE=xsuaa`):
 - `XSUAA_URL`, `XSUAA_CLIENT_ID`, `XSUAA_CLIENT_SECRET`, `XSUAA_TOKEN_URL`

